 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Layer 3: Classical Shadows — Rényi Entropy & Multi-Observable Estimation\n",
    "\n",
    "**Method**: Random Pauli measurements (Huang, Kueng, Preskill 2020; Nature Comm. 2025)\n",
    "\n",
    "For each shadow: apply a random single-qubit Clifford ($X$/$Y$/$Z$ basis per qubit), then measure. From $O(\\log M / \\varepsilon^2)$ shadows, estimate $M$ Pauli observables simultaneously — **independent of system size $n$**.\n",
    "\n",
    "### What we demonstrate here\n",
    "1. **Rényi-2 entropy** $S_2(\\rho_A) = -\\log_2 \\text{Tr}(\\rho_A^2)$: positive value proves entanglement across the bipartition $A|\\bar{A}$\n",
    "2. **Sample complexity advantage**: estimating $M$ witness observables from $O(\\log M)$ shadows vs $O(M)$ traditional circuits\n",
    "3. **Variety**: a completely different mathematical framework from Bell inequalities"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, '..')\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from src.backend import get_backend\n",
    "\n",
    "import os\n",
    "TOKEN = os.environ.get('IQM_TOKEN', None)\n",
    "backend = get_backend(token=TOKEN, device='emerald')\n",
    "print(f'Backend: {backend}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Shadow Tomography on GHZ State\n",
    "\n",
    "We first validate the protocol on a GHZ state, where we know the expected entanglement structure."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from src.witnesses.classical_shadows import run_shadows, estimate_pauli_expval, renyi2_entropy\n",
    "from src.circuits.ghz import build_ghz_no_measure\n",
    "\n",
    "N_QUBITS = 6\n",
    "NUM_SHADOWS = 500   # batched into groups of 200\n",
    "SHOTS_PER = 20\n",
    "\n",
    "ghz = build_ghz_no_measure(N_QUBITS)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Define bipartitions to measure entanglement across\n",
    "subsystems = [\n",
    "    list(range(1)),             # 1-qubit cut\n",
    "    list(range(2)),             # 2-qubit cut\n",
    "    list(range(N_QUBITS//2)),   # half-system cut\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "result = run_shadows(backend, ghz, num_shadows=NUM_SHADOWS,\n",
    "                     shots_per_shadow=SHOTS_PER,\n",
    "                     subsystems=subsystems, seed=42)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Classical shadows on GHZ-{N_QUBITS}:')\n",
    "print(f'  Total shots used: {NUM_SHADOWS * SHOTS_PER}')\n",
    "print()\n",
    "for sub_key, purity in result['purities'].items():\n",
    "    s2 = result['renyi2'][sub_key]\n",
    "    print(f'  Subsystem {sub_key}:')\n",
    "    print(f'    Purity Tr(ρ²) = {purity:.4f}  (1.0 = pure, 0.5 = max mixed for 1 qubit)')\n",
    "    print(f'    Rényi-2 entropy S₂ = {s2:.4f}  (> 0 → entanglement proven)')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Shadow Tomography on Cluster State"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from src.circuits.cluster_2d import build_cluster_2d_no_measure\n",
    "\n",
    "ROWS, COLS = 3, 4  # 12 qubits\n",
    "n = ROWS * COLS\n",
    "cluster = build_cluster_2d_no_measure(ROWS, COLS)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Bipartitions at different scales\n",
    "subsystems_cluster = [\n",
    "    list(range(1)),\n",
    "    list(range(COLS)),        # one full row\n",
    "    list(range(n//2)),        # half system\n",
    "    list(range(ROWS*COLS//3)),# one third\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "result_cluster = run_shadows(backend, cluster, num_shadows=NUM_SHADOWS,\n",
    "                              shots_per_shadow=SHOTS_PER,\n",
    "                              subsystems=subsystems_cluster, seed=123)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Classical shadows on {ROWS}x{COLS} cluster state:')\n",
    "for sub_key, purity in result_cluster['purities'].items():\n",
    "    s2 = result_cluster['renyi2'][sub_key]\n",
    "    print(f'  Subsystem {sub_key}: S₂ = {s2:.4f}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Estimating Pauli Expectation Values\n",
    "\n",
    "Demonstrate that shadows allow estimating **many observables at once**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from src.witnesses.classical_shadows import estimate_pauli_expval\n",
    "\n",
    "snapshots = result['snapshots']\n",
    "\n",
    "# Estimate XX...X (all-X Pauli) — should be ≈ 1 for GHZ state\n",
    "all_x = tuple('X' for _ in range(N_QUBITS))\n",
    "xx_val = estimate_pauli_expval(snapshots, all_x)\n",
    "print(f'⟨X^⊗{N_QUBITS}⟩ = {xx_val:.4f}  (expect +1 for GHZ)')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Estimate individual Z's — should be ≈ 0 for GHZ\n",
    "for q in range(min(3, N_QUBITS)):\n",
    "    pauli = tuple('Z' if i == q else 'I' for i in range(N_QUBITS))\n",
    "    val = estimate_pauli_expval(snapshots, pauli)\n",
    "    print(f'⟨Z_{q}⟩ = {val:.4f}  (expect 0 for GHZ)')\n",
    "\n",
    "# ZZ correlations — should be ≈ 1 for GHZ (all qubits correlated)\n",
    "zz = tuple('Z' if i in [0, N_QUBITS-1] else 'I' for i in range(N_QUBITS))\n",
    "zz_val = estimate_pauli_expval(snapshots, zz)\n",
    "print(f'⟨Z₀ Z_{N_QUBITS-1}⟩ = {zz_val:.4f}  (expect +1 for GHZ)')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Sample Complexity: Shadows vs Traditional Tomography"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Demonstrate scaling advantage\n",
    "qubit_sizes = [2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12]\n",
    "M_observables = 100  # number of Pauli observables to estimate\n",
    "\n",
    "shadows_shots = [int(np.ceil(np.log2(M_observables) / 0.01)) for _ in qubit_sizes]  # O(log M)\n",
    "traditional_shots = [3**n * 100 for n in qubit_sizes]   # O(3^n) for full tomography\n",
    "direct_shots = [M_observables * 1000 for _ in qubit_sizes]  # O(M) separate measurements\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(9, 5))\n",
    "ax.semilogy(qubit_sizes, shadows_shots, 'o-', color='#32a8a4', linewidth=2,\n",
    "            markersize=8, label=f'Classical Shadows (O(log M), M={M_observables})')\n",
    "ax.semilogy(qubit_sizes, direct_shots, 's--', color='#e84545', linewidth=2,\n",
    "            markersize=8, label=f'Direct measurement (O(M) circuits)')\n",
    "ax.semilogy(qubit_sizes, traditional_shots, '^:', color='gray', linewidth=2,\n",
    "            markersize=8, label='Full tomography (O(3^n))')\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('Number of qubits')\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel('Total shots needed')\n",
    "ax.set_title(f'Sample Complexity: Classical Shadows vs Traditional Methods\\n'\n",
    "             f'Estimating {M_observables} Pauli observables simultaneously')\n",
    "ax.legend()\n",
    "ax.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig('shadows_scaling.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Rényi entropy vs subsystem size (area law check)\n",
    "cluster_4x4 = build_cluster_2d_no_measure(4, 4)  # 16 qubits\n",
    "cut_sizes = list(range(1, 9))\n",
    "subsystems_cut = [list(range(k)) for k in cut_sizes]\n",
    "\n",
    "result_area = run_shadows(backend, cluster_4x4, num_shadows=600,\n",
    "                           shots_per_shadow=20,\n",
    "                           subsystems=subsystems_cut, seed=999)\n",
    "\n",
    "entropies = [result_area['renyi2'][str(list(range(k)))] for k in cut_sizes]\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 4))\n",
    "ax.plot(cut_sizes, entropies, 'o-', color='#32a8a4', linewidth=2, markersize=8)\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('Subsystem size |A|')\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel('Rényi-2 entropy S₂(ρ_A)')\n",
    "ax.set_title('Entanglement Entropy vs Subsystem Size (4×4 Cluster State)\\n'\n",
    "             'Non-zero values prove entanglement across every bipartition')\n",
    "ax.axhline(0, color='red', linestyle=':', label='S=0 (no entanglement)')\n",
    "ax.legend()\n",
    "ax.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig('shadows_entropy.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print('S₂ > 0 for all bipartitions:', all(e > 0 for e in entropies))"
   ]
  }
